        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x+5y-14=0$",
          "worked": "Using $R(7,0)$ and $m=-\\frac25$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-0&=-\\frac25(x-7)\\\\5y&=-2x+14\\\\2x+5y-14&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the equations of the other two medians of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5x-4y-13=0$ and $y=-7x+27$.\n\nFind the midpoint of each opposite side, then use the gradient and the corresponding vertex.",
          "worked": "Let $T$ be the midpoint of $QR$.\n$$\\begin{align*}T&=\\left(\\frac{3+7}{2},\\frac{6+0}{2}\\right)\\\\T&=(5,3)\\\\m_{PT}&=\\frac{3-(-2)}{5-1}\\\\m_{PT}&=\\frac54\\end{align*}$$\nThe median through $P(1,-2)$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}y+2&=\\frac54(x-1)\\\\4y+8&=5x-5\\\\5x-4y-13&=0\\end{align*}$$\nLet $U$ be the midpoint of $PR$.\n$$\\begin{align*}U&=\\left(\\frac{1+7}{2},\\frac{-2+0}{2}\\right)\\\\U&=(4,-1)\\\\m_{QU}&=\\frac{-1-6}{4-3}\\\\m_{QU}&=-7\\end{align*}$$\nThe median through $Q(3,6)$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}y-6&=-7(x-3)\\\\y-6&=-7x+21\\\\y&=-7x+27\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
